.TH OMZTTY 1 "2026-11" "oh-my-ztty" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
omztty \- a lean Project Z terminal workspace
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omztty
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Launches a preset zsh environment in the current terminal or bundled ztty.
Manage environment variables, PATH, zsh snippets and application profiles from
one command. Shared configuration lives in the editable profile. A profile with
its own Git repository records managed shared shell changes as local commits;
push is explicit. Machine-specific values remain local.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B shell
Run zsh with the suite configuration. Additional arguments are passed to zsh.
.TP
.B terminal
Open ztty running the suite shell. Additional arguments are ztty options.
.TP
.B setup [\-\-local | \-\-repo NAME | \-\-from OWNER/NAME] [\-\-yes] [\-\-install-rc]
Guide local configuration and optional private GitHub profile synchronization.
The interactive wizard asks before connecting the normal zsh startup file or
creating a remote repository. Remote setup uses the current GitHub CLI account.
\-\-local initializes local configuration; \-\-repo creates a private repository;
\-\-from restores an existing private repository into an absent profile location.
\-\-install-rc explicitly installs the zsh loader block. \-\-yes requires an
explicit local, create or restore choice.
.TP
.B env list [\-\-show]
List saved variable names and scopes. Values are hidden unless requested.
.TP
.B env set NAME VALUE [\-\-shared]
Save a machine-specific environment value. \-\-shared saves it in the profile.
Local values take priority over shared values with the same name.
.TP
.B env get NAME
Print the saved value explicitly.
.TP
.B env unset NAME [\-\-shared]
Remove the saved definition in the selected scope.
.TP
.B env file [\-\-shared]
Print the environment file's actual location.
.TP
.B env edit [\-\-shared]
Open the environment file with the configured editor.
.TP
.B path list [\-\-effective]
List saved PATH rules, or inspect the PATH inherited by this command.
.TP
.B path add DIR [\-\-prepend | \-\-append]
Save a directory rule. Prepending is the default; appending places it after the
inherited PATH. Paths under HOME are stored in portable form. Quote spaces.
.TP
.B path remove DIR
Remove a saved rule. The same directory may still be supplied by another source.
.TP
.B path move DIR first|last
Move a saved directory to the first or last position.
.TP
.B path file
Print the PATH rules file's actual location.
.TP
.B path edit
Open the PATH rules file with the configured editor.
.TP
.B rc init
Prepare the standard profile and shell configuration layout.
.TP
.B rc status
Print the rc entry, shared and local configuration paths, active history mode
and an explicit reload command for the current zsh.
.TP
.B rc list
List saved zsh snippets and their enabled state.
.TP
.B rc add NAME [\-\-from FILE]
Create a snippet or import an existing zsh file.
.TP
.B rc edit NAME
Edit a snippet with the configured editor.
.TP
.B rc show NAME
Print a snippet's contents.
.TP
.B rc enable NAME | rc disable NAME | rc remove NAME
Enable, disable or remove a saved snippet.
.TP
.B rc check
Check saved shell configuration and snippet syntax without executing snippets.
.TP
.B rc file [NAME]
Print the snippet directory or a named snippet's path.
.TP
.B rc install [\-\-dry-run]
Add the managed loader block to ZDOTDIR/.zshrc, or HOME/.zshrc when ZDOTDIR is
unset. Preserve the existing startup code. Repeated installation keeps one block.
.TP
.B rc uninstall [\-\-dry-run]
Remove the managed loader block while retaining saved configuration.
.TP
.B rc backups
List local file snapshots when the profile has no Git repository. With profile
Git enabled, direct the user to sync history. New snapshots stop in Git mode.
.TP
.B rc restore BACKUP_ID
Restore a selected local file snapshot before Git is enabled, preserving the
current file first. An absence record removes the file created after that
record. With profile Git enabled, use sync restore instead.
.TP
.B config
Manage the application profile through zdot. Actions include init, plan, apply,
status, remove, refresh, audit and path. Apply accepts \-\-backup to preserve
existing configurations. Refresh updates unchanged shipped defaults.
.TP
.B sync init
Initialize an independent Git repository in the existing profile and record its
initial configuration, without creating a remote or pushing. Git becomes the
history for managed shared shell changes, and new local file snapshots stop. Use setup for guided private GitHub creation or
restoration. Configure Git user.name and user.email for local commits.
.TP
.B sync status|pull|push
Inspect or synchronize the standard profile repository. Status is local.
Pull requires a clean tree and only fast-forwards. Managed shared shell edits
already have local commits; push also commits remaining allowed changes,
including manual edits, and uploads them to the verified private repository.
Only allowed text configuration is synchronized. Configuration is not executed
or deployed by a sync operation. config sync is an alias.
.TP
.B sync history
Show the latest 20 local commits with short identifiers, dates and subjects.
No network operation is performed.
.TP
.B sync restore REV [PATH]
Restore shared shell configuration from REV, or one allowed file named by its
path relative to the profile. Without PATH the scope is shell/, including
shared environment values, PATH rules and rc snippets. A clean working tree
is required. Validate the selected configuration and record the restoration
as a new local commit, without a backup or push. A currently tracked file
absent from REV is removed when explicitly selected.
.TP
.B ai
Connect the current directory using bundled ssmcp.
.TP
.B dot
Run bundled zdot for independently managed deployments.
.TP
.B zshard
Manage shell plugins.
.TP
.B doctor
Check system and bundled components without connecting to a remote service.
.TP
.B update [\-\-desktop | \-\-no-desktop] [\-\-with-config]
Install the latest published per-user release, verifying its checksum.
\-\-with-config also pulls the configured profile repository.
The saved desktop entry choice is preserved unless explicitly changed.
\-\-desktop enables the managed entry; \-\-no-desktop removes only a link
that still points to this suite. Foreign files and links are preserved.
The preference is saved only after installation succeeds.
.TP
.B update \-\-config-only
Pull the configured profile repository without replacing the suite runtime.
.TP
.B uninstall
Remove suite-owned runtime files and links. Preserve user configuration and history.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
omztty setup \-\-local
omztty env set EDITOR nvim \-\-shared
omztty path add "$HOME/.local/bin"
omztty rc add aliases
omztty rc edit aliases
omztty rc check
omztty rc install \-\-dry-run
omztty rc install
omztty shell
.fi
.PP
New shell sessions load saved changes. To reload from an existing suite shell:
.nf
source "$OMZTTY_ROOT/config/zsh/settings.zsh"
.fi
.PP
Reloading also runs enabled rc snippets again. A command cannot modify the
parent shell's environment; use a fresh shell to check removed settings.
.SH FILES
The following paths use the default XDG roots. env file, path file, rc file and
config path print the configured locations.
.TP
.I ~/.config/oh-my-ztty/profile/
Editable profile repository, application configuration and profile.zdot mappings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/oh-my-ztty/profile/shell/env.tsv
Shared environment values, one NAME, tab and literal VALUE per line.
.TP
.I ~/.config/oh-my-ztty/profile/shell/path.tsv
Ordered PATH rules, one prepend or append, tab and directory per line.
.TP
.I ~/.config/oh-my-ztty/profile/shell/rc.d/
Shared zsh snippets.
.TP
.I ~/.config/oh-my-ztty/local/env.tsv
Machine-specific environment values, outside the synchronized profile.
.TP
.I ~/.config/oh-my-ztty/options.zsh
Local options loaded before zshard initialization.
.TP
.I ~/.config/oh-my-ztty/local.zsh
Existing local shell additions. XDG_CONFIG_HOME is respected.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/oh-my-ztty
Versioned runtime. XDG_DATA_HOME is respected.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/oh-my-ztty/backups/
File snapshots made before profile Git was enabled. Enabling Git retains old
snapshots and stops new ones, including for machine-specific environment values
and the home rc file. Those local files remain outside Git.
XDG_STATE_HOME is respected.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/oh-my-ztty/history
Shell history.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/zdot/oh-my-ztty/
Application deployment journal and saved originals.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zsh (1),
.BR git (1),
.BR gh (1),
.BR zdot (1),
.BR ssmcp (1)
